# bashy verified build declaration for klatch (builds/README.md).
# Shell-sourceable KEY=VALUE only. builds/render.sh renders ../fork from this
# file + files/ + build.yml + audit.yml + builds/_shared, and ships it
# verbatim as the fork's bashy-build/PIN. The workflow refuses to build
# unless the checked-out upstream tag resolves to UPSTREAM_COMMIT and the
# bashy tag is bashy-${UPSTREAM_TAG}-N.
#
# Klatch is bashy's rebrand of Databag (github.com/balzack/databag,
# Apache-2.0, by Roland Osborne — see README.md #Credit), carried on OUR OWN
# fork github.com/qiangli/klatch. There is no third-party "upstream release"
# to mirror here, so UPSTREAM_REPO/UPSTREAM_SLUG name that same fork, and
# bashy plays both roles (the pinned source AND the build fork) the way
# every other tool's UPSTREAM_SLUG/FORK_REPO split two different repos.
# The ONE pin field is UPSTREAM_COMMIT; the manager bumps it to the eventual
# rebrand commit and cuts a matching UPSTREAM_TAG release — see README.md
# #Pin provenance.
TOOL=klatch
FORK_REPO=qiangli/klatch
UPSTREAM_REPO=https://github.com/qiangli/klatch
UPSTREAM_SLUG=qiangli/klatch
# v1.2.2 is an annotated tag WE cut on qiangli/klatch at UPSTREAM_COMMIT,
# with a non-draft, non-prerelease GitHub Release — the same "pin job
# queries the release API" shape every tool uses, just with us as the
# release author (balzack/databag itself cuts no releases at all). The fork
# also carries an unrelated 2022 upstream tag v0.1.0 (pre-rebrand, from
# before this fork existed) — that tag is NOT this build's pin and must
# never be used here. See README.md #Pin provenance for the exact operator
# step that cut v1.2.2.
UPSTREAM_TAG=v1.2.2
UPSTREAM_COMMIT=43ba796aa15cfae99858a6872d36b87b33bdeab6
# Toolchain kind: the repo builds TWO different artifact shapes from one
# matrix — a cgo Go server per linux arch (net/server), and one
# architecture-independent Node/yarn web bundle (app/client/web) — so
# setup+build+audit are all klatch's own (build.yml, audit.yml next to this
# file); no builds/_shared/kinds/custom exists to inherit from.
KIND=custom
# net/server/go.mod at this commit names `go 1.23.0` / `toolchain go1.24.5`,
# both EOL (Go ships security fixes for only its two newest minors) with no
# later upstream commit yet carrying a newer one. Same EOL-minor security
# override shape builds/_shared/kinds/go uses (README.md #Recorded security
# overrides): move to the oldest currently supported minor's latest patch.
GO_TOOLCHAIN=1.26.9
# Node 22 + classic Yarn: upstream Dockerfile builds app/client/web FROM
# node:22-alpine with `yarn --frozen-lockfile && yarn run build`. Upstream
# pins neither Node's patch nor Yarn's version; these are bashy's own
# reviewed pins, same shape as gitea's NODE_VERSION/PNPM_VERSION.
NODE_VERSION=22
YARN_VERSION=1.22.22
GOVULNCHECK_VERSION=v1.9.0
COSIGN_VERSION=v3.1.3
# Build matrix: ASSET=RUNNER; each leg uploads out/ASSET. The MVP deploy
# host is macOS arm64 (see README.md #MVP scope), so the server is built
# natively for linux amd64+arm64 AND darwin arm64+amd64 (windows later); the
# web bundle is architecture-independent and built once. build.yml's Go
# build step is already OS-agnostic (it branches only on matrix.asset being
# the web leg or not), so the darwin legs need no build-step changes — only
# the matrix entries and the native-clang host dependency below.
MATRIX="klatch-$UPSTREAM_TAG-linux-amd64.tar.gz=ubuntu-24.04 klatch-$UPSTREAM_TAG-linux-arm64.tar.gz=ubuntu-24.04-arm klatch-$UPSTREAM_TAG-darwin-arm64.tar.gz=macos-15 klatch-$UPSTREAM_TAG-darwin-amd64.tar.gz=macos-15-intel klatch-web-$UPSTREAM_TAG.tar.gz=ubuntu-24.04"
# build-essential: the cgo link (gorm's sqlite driver, mattn/go-sqlite3,
# needs a C compiler — upstream Dockerfile's build-base). strace/util-linux/
# iproute2/curl: the no-egress gate. Linux only (bashy-build.yml gates this
# install step on runner.os == 'Linux'); the macos-15/macos-15-intel runners
# supply their own native clang (Xcode Command Line Tools, preinstalled) for
# the same CGO_ENABLED=1 link, so no darwin host-dependency step is needed.
APT_PACKAGES="build-essential strace util-linux iproute2 curl"
PRE_BUILD_GATES=""
# Shared helper scripts copied from builds/_shared into bashy-build/.
SHARED_FILES="egress-verdict.sh"
# Argument of bashy-build/no-egress-test.sh (a GitHub expression is allowed).
EGRESS_TARGET='out/${{ matrix.asset }}'
# Release: SRC=ASSET copies from bashy-build/, the assets that must exist,
# the ones that are executables, and the release-notes lines.
RELEASE_EXTRA="PIN=klatch-pin.txt otel.env=klatch-otel.env no-tracking.env=klatch-no-tracking.env"
RELEASE_ASSETS="klatch-$UPSTREAM_TAG-linux-amd64.tar.gz klatch-$UPSTREAM_TAG-linux-arm64.tar.gz klatch-$UPSTREAM_TAG-darwin-arm64.tar.gz klatch-$UPSTREAM_TAG-darwin-amd64.tar.gz klatch-web-$UPSTREAM_TAG.tar.gz klatch-$UPSTREAM_TAG.govulncheck.json klatch-web-$UPSTREAM_TAG.yarn-audit.json klatch-pin.txt klatch-otel.env klatch-no-tracking.env"
# Tarballs, not raw binaries: the binary inside is already +x when tarred.
RELEASE_EXECUTABLES=""
RELEASE_NOTE="The server links no update checker, telemetry or analytics code (reviewed at net/server/go.mod); OTel points only at bashy's local collector 127.0.0.1:31415, should an SDK ever be added (it has none today, see files/otel.env). Each linux/darwin arch ships the cgo server binary plus the net/transform asset-processing scripts in one tarball; the web UI bundle ships separately as klatch-web-$UPSTREAM_TAG.tar.gz, the same static files for every arch. The no-egress runtime gate (below) only runs on the linux legs; the darwin tarballs ship without it (see README.md #No-egress gate)."
RELEASE_GATES="pinned commit, CGO sqlite build for linux amd64+arm64 and darwin arm64+amd64 (EOL-minor Go toolchain override go1.26.9; darwin links the runner's native clang), frozen yarn install for the web bundle, govulncheck report (informational: reachable findings are recorded, never gated or waived), yarn audit report (informational, same policy), no-egress (linux server legs only — see README.md #No-egress gate)."
